      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"old money\" Western consumer often values subtle, inherited class signaling—their luxury is quiet, understated, and speaks to lineage. In contrast, the affluent Asian consumer often views luxury through a lens of visible achievement and status affirmation; the brand must loudly declare success. Therefore, your ads for the Western segment should lean into timeless, muted aesthetics and heritage storytelling. For the Asian segment, the visuals need to be more polished, high-impact, and clearly communicate peak modern success and aspiration.",
